# Backend overview

Vertical slice: `packages/server/src/modules/{context}/`.

```text
contract → router → api → use-case → repository | service | port→adapter
                              ↓
                     entity / factory / mapper
```

| Layer       | Path                                      | Rule                               |
| ----------- | ----------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |
| Contract    | `{context}.contract.ts`                   | [router](./router.mdc)             |
| Router      | `{context}.router.ts`                     | [router](./router.mdc)             |
| API         | `{context}.api.ts`                        | [api](./api.mdc)                   |
| Application | `application/{verb}.use-case.ts`          | [application](./application.mdc)   |
| Entity      | `entity/{aggregate}.*`                    | [entity](./entity.mdc)             |
| Repository  | `repository/{aggregate}.repository.ts`    | [repository](./repository.mdc)     |
| Service     | `service/{context}.service.ts`            | [service](./service.mdc)           |
| Port        | consumer `port/{aggregate}.port.ts`       | [port-adapter](./port-adapter.mdc) |
| Adapter     | provider `adapter/{aggregate}.adapter.ts` | [port-adapter](./port-adapter.mdc) |
| Shared      | `src/shared/`                             | [shared](./shared.mdc)             |

## Rules

- Every use-case is an endpoint: same verb on contract, router, and api. See [application](./application.mdc).
- Return the aggregate or the list. No endpoint that exists to read one field (`findOrganizationName`). See [application](./application.mdc).
- Depend inward only (table, top → bottom).
- One aggregate per repository. Another module's data comes through its port (its DTO); then your repository loads your rows.
- No cross-module repo imports — use a port.
- Zod: `@workspace/validation`. Routers `implement` the contract; lower layers do not import oRPC.
- Naming: [naming](../common/naming.mdc) (singular).

## Where logic goes

| Kind                             | Put in                           |
| -------------------------------- | -------------------------------- |
| Workflow, policy, AppError       | [application](./application.mdc) |
| Invariants of one model (no I/O) | [entity](./entity.mdc)           |
| Hash, crypto                     | [service](./service.mdc)         |
| Persist / load this aggregate    | [repository](./repository.mdc)   |
| Read that needs another module   | their port, then your use-case   |

Never in router or api.
